---
import '../styles/article.css';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaButton from '../components/CtaButton.astro';
import StickyBar from '../components/StickyBar.astro';

const title = 'Best Non-Repainting Forex Indicators (2026 Truth)';
const description =
	'Repainting indicators look perfect in history and change after the candle closes. Here is how that happens, how to test it, and where Goldeneye 2.0 fits. The no-repaint claim still needs a demo check.';
const canonicalURL = 'https://www.profitgoldeneye.info/best-non-repainting-forex-indicators';

const options = [
	{
		place: 'The tool to test',
		name: 'The Profit Goldeneye 2.0',
		id: 'goldeneye',
		top: true,
		copy: 'Goldeneye is built around current momentum. SIGHT, FORCE, and PULSE read direction, strength, and timing on the live panel instead of forecasting a future arrow. The creator claims the signals do not repaint. That claim is not a lab certificate. Put it on a demo chart, mark an EXCELLENT signal, and see if it is still there after the next candles close.',
	},
	{
		place: 'Alternative',
		name: 'Fixed support and resistance',
		id: 'support-resistance',
		top: false,
		copy: 'A level you draw and leave alone does not recalculate. Price can slice through it. The line itself does not quietly move after you lose. That stability is the point.',
	},
	{
		place: 'Alternative',
		name: 'Price action',
		id: 'price-action',
		top: false,
		copy: 'Closed candles, swings, and session highs do not repaint. They also do not grade themselves. You supply the read. That is slower than a dashboard and harder to fake in hindsight.',
	},
	{
		place: 'Alternative',
		name: 'A closed-candle rule',
		id: 'closed-candle',
		top: false,
		copy: 'If you only act after a bar closes, you stop trading the signal that existed for thirty seconds and then vanished. Any indicator, including Goldeneye, should be judged on closed bars first.',
	},
];

const faqs = [
	{
		q: 'What is a repainting indicator?',
		a: 'It changes a signal after you could have acted on it. The past chart looks clean because the bad arrows were deleted or moved once the candle closed or new price arrived.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Why do indicators repaint?',
		a: 'The formula runs again when the current bar updates or when it closes. If the code is allowed to rewrite older signals, history stops matching what you saw live. That is a calculation choice, not a market fact.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Does Goldeneye 2.0 repaint?',
		a: 'The creator claims it does not. This page does not treat that as proven. The panel is a live momentum read, which is the right kind of design, and you should still confirm it on a demo before you trust an EXCELLENT grade with real size.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What should I use if I refuse every signal tool?',
		a: 'Fixed support and resistance, price action, and a rule that you only enter after a candle closes. None of those redraw themselves. They also do not rank the setup for you.',
	},
];

const schema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@graph': [
		{
			'@type': 'ItemList',
			name: 'Non-repainting approaches for forex charts',
			itemListOrder: 'https://schema.org/ItemListOrderAscending',
			numberOfItems: options.length,
			itemListElement: options.map((item, index) => ({
				'@type': 'ListItem',
				position: index + 1,
				name: item.name,
				url: `${canonicalURL}#${item.id}`,
			})),
		},
		{
			'@type': 'FAQPage',
			mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({
				'@type': 'Question',
				name: faq.q,
				acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.a },
			})),
		},
	],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalURL={canonicalURL} schema={schema}>
	<div class="article-page">
		<section class="hero">
			<div class="container crumbs">
				<Breadcrumbs
					items={[
						{ label: 'Home', href: '/' },
						{ label: 'Non-repainting indicators', href: '/best-non-repainting-forex-indicators' },
					]}
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="container hero-copy">
				<p class="kicker">2026 truth</p>
				<h1>Best Non-Repainting Forex Indicators (2026 Truth)</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Repainting is the biggest scam in Forex indicators. The history looks perfect. Live, the signal
					changes after the candle closes.
				</p>
				<CtaButton class="btn-lg">Test Goldeneye 2.0 on the live chart →</CtaButton>
				<p class="crosslinks">
					<a href="/">Read the <strong>Goldeneye 2.0 Review</strong> →</a>
					<a href="/profit-goldeneye-pricing">See <strong>Goldeneye 2.0 Pricing</strong> →</a>
					<a href="/profit-goldeneye-bonus">Claim the <strong>Exclusive Bonuses</strong> →</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="band">
			<div class="container narrow">
				<h2>Why the backtest looks better than your trades</h2>
				<p>
					An indicator looks perfect in history, but fails live because it changes its signal after the candle
					closes. You remember a buy arrow. The chart later shows nothing, or it shows the arrow one bar
					earlier, where it would have worked.
				</p>
				<p>
					It happens because the algorithm runs again. While a candle is open, price is still changing, so
					the code recalculates. Honest tools freeze the signal when the bar closes. Repainting tools are
					allowed to rewrite older marks, so the past is always edited to look right.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<CtaButton class="btn-lg">Stop trusting redrawn arrows →</CtaButton>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="band band-alt">
			<div class="container narrow">
				<h2>Where Goldeneye 2.0 fits</h2>
				<p>
					Goldeneye relies on current momentum. SIGHT, FORCE, and PULSE describe direction, strength, and
					timing now. That is a different job from predicting the next candle and then deleting the
					prediction when it fails.
				</p>
				<p>
					The creator claims no repainting. Take that as a claim. Users should test it on a demo first: mark
					the signal, let three candles close, and see if the mark moved. If it moved, it is not the tool this
					page is willing to recommend.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<CtaButton class="btn-lg">Get Goldeneye 2.0 and test the claim →</CtaButton>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="band">
			<div class="container">
				<h2>Other ways to avoid the trap</h2>
				<p class="section-lead">
					If you will not trust a signal tool until you have watched it live, these three do not redraw
					themselves.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<CtaButton class="btn-lg">Or get the panel and test it →</CtaButton>
				</div>
				<div class="rank-list">
					{
						options.map((item) => (
							<article class:list={['rank', item.top && 'rank-top']} id={item.id}>
								<p class="place">{item.place}</p>
								<h3>{item.name}</h3>
								<p>{item.copy}</p>
							</article>
						))
					}
				</div>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<CtaButton class="btn-lg">Get the momentum panel →</CtaButton>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="band band-alt" id="faq">
			<div class="container narrow">
				<h2>Repainting questions</h2>
				<div class="faq-list">
					{
						faqs.map((faq, index) => (
							<details name="repaint-faq" open={index === 0}>
								<summary>{faq.q}</summary>
								<p>{faq.a}</p>
							</details>
						))
					}
				</div>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<CtaButton class="btn-lg">Get Goldeneye 2.0 for $329 →</CtaButton>
				</div>
				<p class="crosslinks">
					<a href="/">Full <strong>review</strong> →</a>
					<a href="/profit-goldeneye-pricing"><strong>Pricing</strong> →</a>
					<a href="/profit-goldeneye-bonus"><strong>Bonuses</strong> →</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
	<StickyBar />
</BaseLayout>
